PHP also supports different databases, including:

* MySQL
* Oracle
* SQL Server

---

# Procedural and Object-Oriented Programming

PHP supports both **procedural programming** and **object-oriented programming (OOP)**.

## Procedural Programming

Code is organized around procedures and functions.

Example:

```php
<?php

function greet() {
    echo "Hello World";
}

greet();

?>
```

## Object-Oriented Programming

Code is organized around classes and objects.

Example:

```php
<?php

class Student {
    public $name;

    public function sayHello() {
        echo "Hello " . $this->name;
    }
}

$student = new Student();
$student->name = "Amran";
$student->sayHello();

?>
```

PHP can also use a mixture of both approaches.

