# PHP + MySQL Architecture

A simple PHP and MySQL application can be represented as:

```text
             USER
               |
               ↓
          WEB BROWSER
               |
               | HTTP Request
               ↓
        APACHE WEB SERVER
               |
               ↓
              PHP
               |
               | SQL
               ↓
             MySQL
               |
               | Data
               ↓
              PHP
               |
               | Response
               ↓
          WEB BROWSER
               |
               ↓
             USER
```

This shows how PHP can act as the connection between the web interface and database.

---

# Example Application Flow

Imagine a student registration system.

The user fills out a form:

```text
Name: Amran
Email: example@email.com
```

The browser sends the form data to the server.

```text
Browser
   ↓
PHP
   ↓
MySQL
```

PHP processes the information and stores it in MySQL.

Later, PHP can retrieve the information:

```text
MySQL
   ↓
PHP
   ↓
HTML
   ↓
Browser
```

The user can then see the stored information.

