#  Conclusion

PHP provides server-side programming capabilities for creating dynamic and interactive web applications, while MySQL provides database functionality for storing and managing data.

With **HTML, CSS, JavaScript, PHP, MySQL, Apache, and XAMPP**, developers can build and test complete web applications locally before deploying them to a production server.

This chapter provides the foundation for the remaining PHP and MySQL topics in the course.
